**Project type:** Beginner-friendly machine-learning cybersecurity demonstration

## Overview

This project trains a Random Forest classifier to distinguish **normal** from **attack-like** network-flow records using eight numeric features. It demonstrates a basic machine-learning workflow: create/load data, split into training and test sets, train a model, evaluate held-out predictions, and save metrics and plots.

> **Important data and safety note:** The included project generates a deterministic **synthetic** dataset locally. It is not captured from a live network, is not a public benchmark, and does not represent real attackers or production traffic. The project performs no scanning, exploitation, packet capture, or network requests. The metrics show that the implementation works on the generated patterns; they must not be interpreted as real-world detection performance.

